{
  "title": "9: al-Tawbah التوبة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بَرَآءَةٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ؕ‏(1)\nBARAAATUN MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI ELAL LAZEENA A’AAHADTTUM MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nA (declaration) of immunity from Allah and His Messenger, to those of the Pagans with whom ye have contracted mutual alliances:- \nفَسِيْحُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ اَرْبَعَةَ اَشْهُرٍ وَّاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِى اللّٰهِۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْزِى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(2)\nFASEEHOOA FIL ARZE ARBA-A’TA ASH-HORINW WWAAA’LAMOOA ANNAKUM GHAYRO MUA’JEZEAA LAAHE WA ANNAL LAAHA MUKHZEAA KAAFEREEN.\nGo ye, then, for four months, backwards and forwards, (as ye will), throughout the land, but know ye that ye cannot frustrate Allah (by your falsehood) but that Allah will cover with shame those who reject Him. \nوَاَذَانٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَى النَّاسِ يَوْمَ الْحَجِّ الْاَكْبَرِ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ بَرِىْۤءٌ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ۙ  وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ ؕ فَاِنْ تُبْتُمْ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِى اللّٰهِ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍۙ‏(3)\nWAAZAANUN MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI ELAL NAASE YAWMA HAJJE WA AL-AAKBARE ANNAL LAAHA BAREAAUN MENAL MUSHREKEEN WA RASOOLUH FA-IN IN TUBTUM FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM WA TAWALLAYTUM FAAA’LAMOOA ANNAKUM GHAYRO MUA’JEZEAA LAAHE WA BASH-SHERIL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-A’ZAABIN A’ZAABAN LEEMIN.\nAnd an announcement from Allah and His Messenger, to the people (assembled) on the day of the Great Pilgrimage, that Allah and His Messenger dissolve (treaty) obligations with the Pagans. If then, ye repent, it were best for you; but if ye turn away, know ye that ye cannot frustrate Allah. And proclaim a grievous penalty to those who reject Faith. \nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَنْقُصُوْكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَمْ يُظَاهِرُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ اَحَدًا فَاَتِمُّوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ عَهْدَهُمْ اِلٰى مُدَّتِهِمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(4)\nILLAA LAZEENA A’AAHADTTUM MENAL MUSHREKEEN SUMMA LAM YANQUSOOKUM SHAY-ANW LAM YUZAAHEROOA A’LAYKUM AHADAN FAATEMMOOA ELAYHIM A’AHDAHUM ELAA MUDDATEHEM INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\n(But the treaties are) not dissolved with those Pagans with whom ye have entered into alliance and who have not subsequently failed you in aught, nor aided any one against you. So fulfil your engagements with them to the end of their term: for Allah loveth the righteous. \nفَاِذَا انْسَلَخَ الْاَشْهُرُ الْحُرُمُ فَاقْتُلُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ حَيْثُ وَجَدْتُّمُوْهُمْ وَخُذُوْهُمْ وَاحْصُرُوْهُمْ وَاقْعُدُوْا لَهُمْ كُلَّ مَرْصَدٍ ۚ فَاِنْ تَابُوْا وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ فَخَلُّوْا سَبِيْلَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(5)\nFA-EZAA ANSALAKHA AL-AASHHURU AL-HURUMU FAAQTULOOA MUSHREKEEN HAYSO WAJADTTUMOOHUM WAKHUZOOHUM WAAHSUROOHUM WAAQU’UDOOA LAHUM KULLA MARSADIN FA-IN TAABOO WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA AAATAWUA ZAKAATA FAKHALLOOA SABEELAHUM INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nBut when the forbidden months are past, then fight and slay the Pagans wherever ye find them, an seize them, beleaguer them, and lie in wait for them in every stratagem (of war); but if they repent, and establish regular prayers and practise regular charity, then open the way for them: for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَاِنْ اَحَدٌ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ اسْتَجَارَكَ فَاَجِرْهُ حَتّٰى يَسْمَعَ كَلَامَ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ اَبْلِغْهُ مَاْمَنَهٗ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(6)\nWA AHAD MENAL MUSHREKEEN ASTAJAARAKA FAAJERHU HATTAA YASMAA’A KALAAMAL LAAHE SUMMA AABLEGHHU MAAMANAH ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUN LAA YA’LAMOON.\nIf one amongst the Pagans ask thee for asylum, grant it to him, so that he may hear the word of Allah; and then escort him to where he can be secure. That is because they are men without knowledge. \nكَيْفَ يَكُوْنُ لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ عَهْدٌ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعِنْدَ رَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ عِنْدَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ فَمَا اسْتَقَامُوْا لَكُمْ فَاسْتَقِيْمُوْا لَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(7)\nKAYFA LAHUL LIL-MUSHREKEENA A’AHDUN I’NDAL LAAHE WA I’NDAL RASOOLEHI ILLAA LAZEENA A’AAHADTTUM I’NDAL MASJEDIL HARAAME FAMAA TATANAZZALO LAKUM FASTAQEEMOO LAHUM INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nHow can there be a league, before Allah and His Messenger, with the Pagans, except those with whom ye made a treaty near the sacred Mosque? As long as these stand true to you, stand ye true to them: for Allah doth love the righteous. \nكَيْفَ وَاِنْ يَّظْهَرُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ لَا يَرْقُبُوْا فِيْكُمْ اِلًّا وَّلَا ذِمَّةً ؕ يُرْضُوْنَكُمْ بِاَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَتَاْبٰى قُلُوْبُهُمْۚ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَۚ‏(8)\nKAYFA WA YYAZHAROOA A’LAYKUM LAA YARQUBOOA FEEKUM AELLAN WA LAA ZEMMATAN YURZOONAKUM BE-AFWAA-HEHIM WATAABAA QULOOBUHUM WA AKSAROHUM FAASEQOONA.\nHow (can there be such a league), seeing that if they get an advantage over you, they respect not in you the ties either of kinship or of covenant? With (fair words from) their mouths they entice you, but their hearts are averse from you; and most of them are rebellious and wicked. \nاِشْتَرَوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا فَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهُمْ سَآءَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(9)\nAESHTARAWA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE SAMANAN QALEELAA FA-SADDU A’N SABEELEH INNAHUM SAAA-A MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThe Signs of Allah have they sold for a miserable price, and (many) have they hindered from His way: evil indeed are the deeds they have done. \nلَا يَرْقُبُوْنَ فِىْ مُؤْمِنٍ اِلًّا وَّلَا ذِمَّةً ؕ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُعْتَدُوْنَ‏(10)\nLAA YARQUBOONA FEE MUMENIN AELLAN WA LAA ZEMMATAN WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL AL-MUA’TADOONA.\nIn a Believer they respect not the ties either of kinship or of covenant! It is they who have transgressed all bounds. \nفَاِنْ تَابُوْا وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ فَاِخْوَانُكُمْ فِى الدِّيْنِؕ وَنُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(11)\nFA-IN TAABOO WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA AATAWUZ ZAKAATA FA-IKHWAANOKUM FIL DEEN WA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nBut (even so), if they repent, establish regular prayers, and practise regular charity, they are your brethren in Faith: (thus) do We explain the Signs in detail, for those who understand. \nوَاِنْ نَّكَثُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ عَهْدِهِمْ وَطَعَنُوْا فِىْ دِيْنِكُمْ فَقَاتِلُوْۤا اَئِمَّةَ الْكُفْرِۙ اِنَّهُمْ لَاۤ اَيْمَانَ لَهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَنْتَهُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA NNAKASOOA AYMAANAHUM MIN BA’DE A’AHDEHEM WATAA’ANOOA FEE DEENEKUM FAQAATELOOA AAEMMATA AL-KUFRE INNAHUM LAA AAYMAANA LAHUM LA-A’LLAHUM YANTAHOONA.\nBut if they violate their oaths after their covenant, and taunt you for your Faith, fight ye the chiefs of Unfaith: for their oaths are nothing to them: that thus they may be restrained. \nاَلَا تُقَاتِلُوْنَ قَوْمًا نَّكَثُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ وَهَمُّوْا بِاِخْرَاجِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَهُمْ بَدَءُوْكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ؕ اَتَخْشَوْنَهُمْ ۚ فَاللّٰهُ اَحَقُّ اَنْ تَخْشَوْهُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(13)\nALAA TUQAATELOONA QAWMAN NNAKASOOA AYMAANAHUM WAHAMMOOA BEAEKHRAAJE RASOOLE WA HUM BADAOOKUM AWWALA MARRAH AATAKHSHAWNAHUM FAL-LAAHO AHAQQO AN TAKHSHAWHU IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nWill ye not fight people who violated their oaths, plotted to expel the Messenger, and took the aggressive by being the first (to assault) you? Do ye fear them? Nay, it is Allah Whom ye should more justly fear, if ye believe! \nقَاتِلُوْهُمْ يُعَذِّبْهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِاَيْدِيْكُمْ وَيُخْزِهِمْ وَيَنْصُرْكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَيَشْفِ صُدُوْرَ قَوْمٍ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(14)\nQAATELOOHUM YUA’AZZEBHUMU LAAHO BE-AYDEEKUM WAYUKHZEHEM WAYANSURKUM A’LAYHIM WAYASHFE SUDOORA QAWMIN MOAMENEEN.\nFight them, and Allah will punish them by your hands, cover them with shame, help you (to victory) over them, heal the breasts of Believers, \nوَيُذْهِبْ غَيْظَ قُلُوْبِهِمْ ؕ وَ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(15)\nWAYUZHEB GHAYZA QOLOOBEHIM WA YATOOBU LAAHO A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd still the indignation of their hearts. For Allah will turn (in mercy) to whom He will; and Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise. \nاَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ اَنْ تُتْرَكُوْا وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ جَاهَدُوْا مِنْكُمْ وَلَمْ يَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا رَسُوْلِهٖ وَلَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَلِيْجَةً ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nAM HASIBTUM AN TUTRAKOOA WA LAMMAA YAA’LAME LAAHO LAZEENA JAAHADOO MINKUM WA LAM YATTAKHEZOOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAA RASOOLEHI WA LAA MOAMENEEN WALEEJATAN WAL LAAHO KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nOr think ye that ye shall be abandoned, as though Allah did not know those among you who strive with might and main, and take none for friends and protectors except Allah, His Messenger, and the (community of) Believers? But Allah is well-acquainted with (all) that ye do. \nمَا كَانَ لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ اَنْ يَّعْمُرُوْا مَسٰجِدَ اللّٰهِ شٰهِدِيْنَ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ بِالكُفْرِؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ ۖۚ وَ فِى النَّارِ هُمْ خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(17)\nMAA KAANA LIL-MUSHREKEENA AN YYAA’MUROOA MANA-A’ LAAHE SHAAHEDEENA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM BEALKUFRE AOOLAAEKA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM WA FIL NAAR HUM KHAALEDOON.\nIt is not for such as join gods with Allah, to visit or maintain the mosques of Allah while they witness against their own souls to infidelity. The works of such bear no fruit: In Fire shall they dwell. \nاِنَّمَا يَعْمُرُ مَسٰجِدَ اللّٰهِ مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَاَ قَامَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَى الزَّكٰوةَ وَلَمْ يَخْشَ اِلَّا اللّٰهَ فَعَسٰٓى اُولٰۤئِكَ اَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مِنَ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(18)\nINNAMAA YAA’MURU MANA-A’ LAAHE MAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA QAAMA SALAATA WA AATAZ ZAKAATA WA LAM YAKHSHA ILLAA LAAHA FA-A’SAA AOOLAAEKA AN YYAKOONOOA MENAL AL-MUHTADEENA.\nThe mosques of Allah shall be visited and maintained by such as believe in Allah and the Last Day, establish regular prayers, and practise regular charity, and fear none (at all) except Allah. It is they who are expected to be on true guidance. \nاَجَعَلْتُمْ سِقَايَةَ الْحَآجِّ وَعِمَارَةَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ كَمَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَجَاهَدَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ لَا يَسْتَوٗنَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۘ‏(19)\nAAJAA’ALTUM SEQAAYATA AL-HAAJJE WAE’EMAARATA MASJEDIL HARAAME KAMAM AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA JAAHADA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE LAA YASTAWNA I’NDAL LAAHE WA LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\n Do ye make the giving of drink to pilgrims, or the maintenance of the Sacred Mosque, equal to (the pious service of) those who believe in Allah and the Last Day, and strive with might and main in the cause of Allah? They are not comparable in the sight of Allah: and Allah guides not those who do wrong. \nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ هَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْۙ اَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً عِنْدَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ‏(20)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM AAA’ZAMU DARAJATAN I’NDAL LAAH WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAAA-EZOON.\nThose who believe, and suffer exile and strive with might and main, in Allah's cause, with their goods and their persons, have the highest rank in the sight of Allah: they are the people who will achieve (salvation). \nيُبَشِّرُهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنْهُ وَرِضْوَانٍ وَّجَنّٰتٍ لَّهُمْ فِيْهَا نَعِيْمٌ مُّقِيْمٌ ۙ‏(21)\nYUBASSHERUHUM RABBOHUM BERAHMATIN MINHO WAREZWAANIN WA LAHUM FEEHAA NAE’EEMUN MMUQEEMUN.\nTheir Lord doth give them glad tidings of a Mercy from Himself, of His good pleasure, and of gardens for them, wherein are delights that endure: \nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عِنْدَهٗۤ اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(22)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM INNAL LAAHA I’NDAHU AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nThey will dwell therein for ever. Verily in Allah's presence is a reward, the greatest (of all). \nيٰۤاَ يُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوْۤا اٰبَآءَكُمْ وَاِخْوَانَكُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ اِنِ اسْتَحَبُّوا الْكُفْرَ عَلَى الْاِيْمَانِ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَوَلَّهُمْ مِّنْكُمْ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(23)\nYAA A’ZAABAN AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA AABAAA-AKUM WAAKHWAANAKUM AAWLEEAAAA ENIS ASTAHABBOOA KUFRA A’LAL AL-AEEMAANE WA MAN YYATAWALLAHUM MINKUM FAAWLAAEKA HOMUL ZAALEMOON.\nO ye who believe! take not for protectors your fathers and your brothers if they love infidelity above Faith: if any of you do so, they do wrong. \nقُلْ اِنْ كَانَ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ وَاَبْنَآؤُكُمْ وَاِخْوَانُكُمْ وَاَزْوَاجُكُمْ وَعَشِيْرَتُكُمْ وَ اَمْوَالُ ۨاقْتَرَفْتُمُوْهَا وَتِجَارَةٌ تَخْشَوْنَ كَسَادَهَا وَ مَسٰكِنُ تَرْضَوْنَهَاۤ اَحَبَّ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَ جِهَادٍ فِىْ سَبِيْلِهٖ فَتَرَ بَّصُوْا حَتّٰى يَاْتِىَ اللّٰهُ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(24)\nQUL IN KAANA AAABAAUKUM WAABNAAUKUM WAAKHWAANUKUM WAAZWAAJUKUM WAA’ASHEERATUKUM WA AAMWAALU AQTARAFTUMOOHAA WATEJAARATUN TAKHSHAWNA KASAADAHAA WA MASAAKENU TARZAWNAHAA AAHABBA ELAYKUM MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA JEHAADIN FEE SABEELEH FA TARA BBASOOA HATTAA HATTAA LAAHO LAAHO WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ FAASEQEEN.\nSay: If it be that your fathers, your sons, your brothers, your mates, or your kindred; the wealth that ye have gained; the commerce in which ye fear a decline: or the dwellings in which ye delight - are dearer to you than Allah, or His Messenger, or the striving in His cause;- then wait until Allah brings about His decision: and Allah guides not the rebellious. \nلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ مَوَاطِنَ كَثِيْرَةٍ ۙ وَّيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ اِذْ اَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ فَلَمْ تُغْنِ عَنْكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّضَاقَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْاَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ ثُمَّ وَلَّيْتُمْ مُّدْبِرِيْنَۚ‏(25)\nLAQAD NASARAKUMU LAAHO FEE MAWAATENA KASEERATIL WWAYAWMA HUNAYNIN IZ A-A’JABATKUM KASRATUKUM FALAM TUGHNE A’NKUM SHAY-ANW WWAZAAQAT A’LAYKOMUL ARZO BEMAA RAHUBAT SUMMA WALLAYTUM MMUDBEREENA.\nAssuredly Allah did help you in many battle-fields and on the day of Hunain: Behold! your great numbers elated you, but they availed you naught: the land, for all that it is wide, did constrain you, and ye turned back in retreat. \nثُمَّ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ سَكِيْنَتَهٗ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَاَنْزَلَ جُنُوْدًا لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا ۚ وَعَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(26)\nSUMMA ANZALAL LAAHO SAKEENATAHU A’LAA RASOOLEHI WA MOAMENEEN WA ANZALA JUNOODAN LAM TARAWHAA WAA’AZZABA LAZEENA KAFAROO WAZAA LEKA JAZAAA-O KAAFEREEN.\nBut Allah did pour His calm on the Messenger and on the Believers, and sent down forces which ye saw not: He punished the Unbelievers; thus doth He reward those without Faith. \nثُمَّ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(27)\nSUMMA YATOOBU LAAHO MIN BA’DE ZAA LEKA A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAgain will Allah, after this, turn (in mercy) to whom He will: for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّمَا الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ نَجَسٌ فَلَا يَقْرَبُوا الْمَسْجِدَ الْحَرَامَ بَعْدَ عَامِهِمْ هٰذَا ۚ وَ اِنْ خِفْتُمْ عَيْلَةً فَسَوْفَ يُغْنِيْكُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖۤ اِنْ شَآءَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(28)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAMAA AL-MUSHREKOONA NAJASUN FALAA YAQRABOOA MASJEDIL HARAAMA BA’DA A’AAMEHEM HAAZAA WA IN KHIFTUM A’AYLATAN FA-SAWFA YUGHNEEKUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI IN SHAAA-AL INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nO ye who believe! Truly the Pagans are unclean; so let them not, after this year of theirs, approach the Sacred Mosque. And if ye fear poverty, soon will Allah enrich you, if He wills, out of His bounty, for Allah is All-knowing, All-wise. \nقَاتِلُوا الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَلَا بِالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَلَا يُحَرِّمُوْنَ مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ وَلَا يَدِيْنُوْنَ دِيْنَ الْحَقِّ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ حَتّٰى يُعْطُوا الْجِزْيَةَ عَنْ يَّدٍ وَّهُمْ صٰغِرُوْنَ‏(29)\nQAATELOOA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA LAA BE-YAWME AAKHERE WA LAA YUHARREMOONA MAA HARRAMA LAAHO WA RASOOLUH WA LAA YADEENOONA DEENA HAQQE MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA HATTAA YUA’TOOA AL-JEZYATA A’N YYADIN WA HUM SAAGHEROON.\nFight those who believe not in Allah nor the Last Day, nor hold that forbidden which hath been forbidden by Allah and His Messenger, nor acknowledge the religion of Truth, (even if they are) of the People of the Book, until they pay the Jizya with willing submission, and feel themselves subdued. \nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ عُزَيْرُ ۨابْنُ اللّٰهِ وَقَالَتِ النَّصٰرَى الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ اللّٰهِؕ ذٰ لِكَ قَوْلُهُمْ بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ ۚ يُضَاهِئُونَ قَوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ قَاتَلَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ۚ اَنّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏‏(30)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO U’UZAYRU ABNU LAAHE WA QAALATIL AN-NASAARAA AL-MASEEHU ABNU LAAH ZAA LEKA QAWLOHUM BE-AFWAAHEKUM FWAAHEHEM YUZAAHEOONA QAWLA LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QABLO QAATALAHUMU LAAHO ANNAA YOAFEKOON.\nThe Jews call 'Uzair a son of Allah, and the Christians call Christ the son of Allah. That is a saying from their mouth; (in this) they but imitate what the unbelievers of old used to say. Allah's curse be on them: how they are deluded away from the Truth! \nاِتَّخَذُوْۤا اَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَانَهُمْ اَرْبَابًا مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمَسِيْحَ ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ ۚ وَمَاۤ اُمِرُوْۤا اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلٰهًا وَّاحِدًا ۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(31)\nITTAKHAZOO AAHBAARAHUM WARUHBAANAHUM AARBAABAN MIN DOONIL LAAHE WAL MASEEHA NA MARYAMAL WA MAA MAAA OMEROO ILLAA LEEA’BUDOOA ELAAHANW WAAHEDANW LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA WALADAN A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nThey take their priests and their anchorites to be their lords in derogation of Allah, and (they take as their Lord) Christ the son of Mary; yet they were commanded to worship but One Allah: there is no god but He. Praise and glory to Him: (Far is He) from having the partners they associate (with Him). \nيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يُّطْفِئُوْا نُوْرَ اللّٰهِ بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ وَيَاْبَى اللّٰهُ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّتِمَّ نُوْرَهٗ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(32)\nYOREEDOONA AN YYUTFEOOA NOORA LAAHE BE-AFWAAHEKUM FWAAHEHEM WAYAABAA LAAHO ILLAA AN YOTIMMAR NOORAH WA LAW KAREHA KAAFEROON.\nFain would they extinguish Allah's light with their mouths, but Allah will not allow but that His light should be perfected, even though the Unbelievers may detest (it). \nهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ رَسُوْلَهٗ بِالْهُدٰى وَدِيْنِ الْحَقِّ لِيُظْهِرَهٗ عَلَى الدِّيْنِ كُلِّهٖۙ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(33)\nHOWA LAZEE ARSALA RASOOLAHU BIL-HODAA WA DEENIL HAQQE LE-YUZHERAHU A’LAL DEENE KULLEH WA LAW KAREHA AL-MUSHREKOONA.\nIt is He Who hath sent His Messenger with guidance and the Religion of Truth, to proclaim it over all religion, even though the Pagans may detest (it). \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ الْاَحْبَارِ وَالرُّهْبَانِ لَيَاْكُلُوْنَ اَمْوَالَ النَّاسِ بِالْبَاطِلِ وَيَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَكْنِزُوْنَ الذَّهَبَ وَالْفِضَّةَ وَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَهَا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِۙ فَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ اَلِيْمٍۙ‏(34)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAL KASEERAA MENAL AL-AAHBAARE WAALRRUHBAANE LAYAAKULOONA AAMWAALA NAASE BIL-BAATELE WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAH WAL LAZEENA YAKNEZOONA AZ-ZAHABA WAL FEZZATA WA LAA YUNFEQOONAHAA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FA-BASH-SHIRHUM BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\n O ye who believe! there are indeed many among the priests and anchorites, who in Falsehood devour the substance of men and hinder (them) from the way of Allah. And there are those who bury gold and silver and spend it not in the way of Allah: announce unto them a most grievous penalty- \nيَّومَ يُحْمٰى عَلَيْهَا فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ فَتُكْوٰى بِهَا جِبَاهُهُمْ وَجُنُوْبُهُمْ وَظُهُوْرُهُمْؕ هٰذَا مَا كَنَزْتُمْ لِاَنْفُسِكُمْ فَذُوْقُوْا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْنِزُوْنَ‏(35)\nYYAWMA YUHMAA A’LAYHAA FEE NAARE JAHANNAMA FATUKWAA BEHAA JEBAAHUHUM WAJUNOOBUHUM WAZUHOORUHUM HAAZAA MAA KANAZTUM MAA TOQADDEMOO FA-ZOOQOO MAA KUNTUM TAKNEZOONA.\nOn the Day when heat will be produced out of that (wealth) in the fire of Hell, and with it will be branded their foreheads, their flanks, and their backs, their flanks, and their backs.- “This is the (treasure) which ye buried for yourselves: taste ye, then, the (treasures) ye buried!” \nاِنَّ عِدَّةَ الشُّهُوْرِ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ اثْنَا عَشَرَ شَهْرًا فِىْ كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِ يَوْمَ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ مِنْهَاۤ اَرْبَعَةٌ حُرُمٌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الدِّيْنُ الْقَيِّمُ ۙ فَلَا تَظْلِمُوْا فِيْهِنَّ اَنْفُسَكُمْ ؕ وَقَاتِلُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ كَآفَّةً كَمَا يُقَاتِلُوْنَكُمْ كَآفَّةً  ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(36)\nINNAL E’EDDATA ASH-SHUHOORE I’NDAL LAAHE ASNAA A’ASHARA SHAHRAN FEE KETAABIL LAAHE YAWMA KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA MINHAA AARBAA’ATUN HURUMUN ZAA LEKA DEENO AL-QAYMU FALAA TAZLEMOOA FEEHINNA ANFOSAKUM WAQAATELOOA MUSHREKEEN KAAAF-FATANW KAMAA YOQAATELOONAKUM KAAAF-FATANW WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA LAAHA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nThe number of months in the sight of Allah is twelve (in a year)- so ordained by Him the day He created the heavens and the earth; of them four are sacred: that is the straight usage. So wrong not yourselves therein, and fight the Pagans all together as they fight you all together. But know that Allah is with those who restrain themselves. \nاِنَّمَا النَّسِىْٓءُ زِيَادَةٌ فِى الْكُفْرِ يُضَلُّ بِهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُحِلُّوْنَهٗ عَامًا وَّيُحَرِّمُوْنَهٗ عَامًا لِّيُوَاطِئُوْا عِدَّةَ مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ فَيُحِلُّوْا مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ ؕ زُيِّنَ لَهُمْ سُوْۤءُ اَعْمَالِهِمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(37)\nINNAMAA AN-NASEAAAAU ZEEADATUN FIL AL-KUFRE YUZALLU BEHIL LAZEENA KAFAROO YUHELLOONAH A’AMAA WWAYUHARREMOONAH A’AMAA LLEEWAATEOOA E’EDDATA MAA HARRAMA LAAHO FAYUHELLOOA MAA HARRAMA LAAHO ZUYYENA LAHUM SOOU AAA’MAALEHEM WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ KAAFEREEN.\nVerily the transposing (of a prohibited month) is an addition to Unbelief: the Unbelievers are led to wrong thereby: for they make it lawful one year, and forbidden another year, in order to adjust the number of months forbidden by Allah and make such forbidden ones lawful. The evil of their course seems pleasing to them. But Allah guideth not those who reject Faith. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَا لَكُمْ اِذَا قِيْلَ لَكُمُ انْفِرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اثَّاقَلْتُمْ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ ؕ اَرَضِيْتُمْ بِالْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا مِنَ الْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ فَمَا مَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ‏(38)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MAA LAKUM EZAA QEELA LAKOMUL ANFEROOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE ASSAAQALTUM ELAL ARZE AARAZEETUM BE-HAYAATID DUNYAA MENAL AAKHERATE FAMAA MATAAU’U HAYAATID DUNYAA FIL AAKHERATE ILLAA QALEELUN.\nO ye who believe! what is the matter with you, that, when ye are asked to go forth in the cause of Allah, ye cling heavily to the earth? Do ye prefer the life of this world to the Hereafter? But little is the comfort of this life, as compared with the Hereafter. \nاِلَّا تَنْفِرُوْا يُعَذِّبْكُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا   ۙ وَّيَسْتَبْدِلْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْ وَلَا تَضُرُّوْهُ شَيْئًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(39)\nILLAA TANFEROOA QABLO A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA WWAYASTABDEL QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM WA LAA TAZURROOHU SHAY-ANW WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nUnless ye go forth, He will punish you with a grievous penalty, and put others in your place; but Him ye would not harm in the least. For Allah hath power over all things. \nاِلَّا تَنْصُرُوْهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللّٰهُ اِذْ اَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ثَانِىَ اثْنَيْنِ اِذْ هُمَا فِى الْغَارِ اِذْ يَقُوْلُ لِصَاحِبِهٖ لَا تَحْزَنْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَنَا ۚ فَاَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ سَكِيْنَتَهٗ عَلَيْهِ وَاَ يَّدَهٗ بِجُنُوْدٍ لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلٰى ؕ وَكَلِمَةُ اللّٰهِ هِىَ الْعُلْيَا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(40)\nILLAA TANSUROOHU FAQAD NASARAHU LAAHO IZ AAKHRAJAHU LAZEENA KAFAROO SAANEAAA NAYNE IZ HUMAA FIL AL-GHAARE IZ YAQOOLO LESAAHEBEH LAA TAHZAN INNAL LAAHA MAA’ANAA FA ANZALAS LAAHO SAKEENATAHU A’LAYHE WA YYADAH BEJONOODIL LAM TARAWHAA WA KALEMATAT LAZEENA KAFARUL AS-SUFLAA WAKALEMATU LAAHE HEYA AL-U’ULYAA WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nIf ye help not (your leader), (it is no matter): for Allah did indeed help him, when the Unbelievers drove him out: he had no more than one companion; they two were in the cave, and he said to his companion, “Have no fear, for Allah is with us”: then Allah sent down His peace upon him, and strengthened him with forces which ye saw not, and humbled to the depths the word of the Unbelievers. But the word of Allah is exalted to the heights: for Allah is Exalted in might, Wise. \nاِنْفِرُوْا خِفَافًا وَّثِقَالًا وَّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِكُمْ وَاَنْفُسِكُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(41)\nAENFEROOA KHEFAAFAN WWASEQAALAN WWAJAAHEDOOA BE-ANWAALEKUM WA ANFOSEKUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE ZAA ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nGo ye forth, (whether equipped) lightly or heavily, and strive and struggle, with your goods and your persons, in the cause of Allah. That is best for you, if ye (but) knew. \nلَوْ كَانَ عَرَضًا قَرِيْبًا وَّسَفَرًا قَاصِدًا لَّاتَّبَعُوْكَ وَلٰكِنْۢ بَعُدَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الشُّقَّةُ  ؕ وَسَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَوِ اسْتَطَعْنَا لَخَرَجْنَا مَعَكُمْ ۚ يُهْلِكُوْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(42)\nLAW KAANA A’ARAZAN QAREEBAA WWASAFARAN QAASEDAN LLAATTABAU’OOKA WA LAAKIL BAU’UDAT A’LAYHEMUL ASH-SHUQQATU WASAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAWE ASTATAA’NAA LAKHARAJNAA MA-A’KUM YUHLEKOONA ANFOSAHUM WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nIf there had been immediate gain (in sight), and the journey easy, they would (all) without doubt have followed thee, but the distance was long, (and weighed) on them. They would indeed swear by Allah, “If we only could, we should certainly have come out with you”: They would destroy their own souls; for Allah doth know that they are certainly lying. \nعَفَا اللّٰهُ عَنْكَۚ لِمَ اَذِنْتَ لَهُمْ حَتّٰى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكَ الَّذِيْنَ صَدَقُوْا وَتَعْلَمَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(43)\nA’AFAA LAAHO A’NKAL LEMA AAZENTA LAHUM HATTAA YATABAYYANA LAKA LAZEENA SADAQOO WATAA’LAMA KAAZEBEEN.\nAllah give thee grace! why didst thou grant them until those who told the truth were seen by thee in a clear light, and thou hadst proved the liars? \nلَا يَسْتَاْذِنُكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ اَنْ يُّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(44)\nLAA YASTAAZENUKA LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE AN YYUJAAHEDOOA BEAAMWAALEHEM WAANFUSEHEM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BE-MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nThose who believe in Allah and the Last Day ask thee for no exemption from fighting with their goods and persons. And Allah knoweth well those who do their duty. \nاِنَّمَا يَسْتَاْذِنُكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَارْتَابَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ فَهُمْ فِىْ رَيْبِهِمْ يَتَرَدَّدُوْنَ‏(45)\nINNAMAA YASTAAZENUKA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WAARTAABAT QULOOBUHUM FAHUM FEE RAYBEHEM YATARADDADOONA.\nOnly those ask thee for exemption who believe not in Allah and the Last Day, and whose hearts are in doubt, so that they are tossed in their doubts to and fro. \nوَلَوْ اَرَادُوْا الْخُرُوْجَ لَاَعَدُّوْا لَهٗ عُدَّةً وَّلٰكِنْ كَرِهَ اللّٰهُ انۢبِعَاثَهُمْ فَثَبَّطَهُمْ وَقِيْلَ اقْعُدُوْا مَعَ الْقٰعِدِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAW AARAADOOA AL-KHUROOJA LAAA’ADDOOA LAHU U’UDDATAN LAAKIL KAREHA LAAHO ANBEA’AASAHUM FASABBATAHUM WA QEELAD AQU’UDOOA LAAHA AL-QAAE’EDEENA.\n If they had intended to come out, they would certainly have made some preparation therefor; but Allah was averse to their being sent forth; so He made them lag behind, and they were told, “Sit ye among those who sit (inactive).” \nلَوْ خَرَجُوْا فِيْكُمْ مَّا زَادُوْكُمْ اِلَّا خَبَالًا وَّلَاْاَوْضَعُوْا خِلٰلَكُمْ يَبْغُوْنَكُمُ الْفِتْنَةَ ۚ وَفِيْكُمْ سَمّٰعُوْنَ لَهُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(47)\nLAW KHARAJOO FEEKUM MAA ZAADOOKUM ILLAA KHABAALAN WWALAAAAWZAU’OOA KHELAALAKUM YABGHOONAKUMU FITNATA WA FEEKUM SAMMAAU’OONA LAHUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nIf they had come out with you, they would not have added to your (strength) but only (made for) disorder, hurrying to and fro in your midst and sowing sedition among you, and there would have been some among you who would have listened to them. But Allah knoweth well those who do wrong. \nلَقَدِ ابْتَغَوُا الْفِتْنَةَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَقَلَّبُوْا لَكَ الْاُمُوْرَ حَتّٰى جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَظَهَرَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ وَهُمْ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(48)\nLAQADE ABTAGHAWUA FITNATA MIN QABLO WAQALLABOOA LAKA AL-AUMOORA HATTAA JAAA-A HAQQO WA ZAHARAL AMRUL LAAHE WA HUM KAAREHOONA.\nIndeed they had plotted sedition before, and upset matters for thee, until, the Truth arrived, and the Decree of Allah became manifest much to their disgust. \nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّقُوْلُ ائْذَنْ لِّىْ وَلَا تَفْتِنِّىْ ؕ اَلَا فِى الْفِتْنَةِ سَقَطُوْا ؕ وَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمُحِيْطَةٌ ۢ بِالْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(49)\nWA MINHUM MAN YAQOOLO AZAN LEE WA LAA TAFTENNEAA ALAA FIL AL-FETNATE SAQATOOA WA INNA JAHANNAMA LA-MOHEETATUM BIL-KAAFEREEN.\nAmong them is (many) a man who says: “Grant me exemption and draw me not into trial.” Have they not fallen into trial already? and indeed Hell surrounds the Unbelievers (on all sides). \nاِنْ تُصِبْكَ حَسَنَةٌ تَسُؤْهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْكَ مُصِيْبَةٌ يَّقُوْلُوْا قَدْ اَخَذْنَاۤ اَمْرَنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَيَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ فَرِحُوْنَ‏(50)\nIN TUSEBKA HASANATUL TASUHUM WA TUSEBKA MUSEEBATUN YAQOOLOO QAD AKHAZNAA AAMRANAA MIN QABLO WAYATAWALLAWA WA HUM FAREEHOON.\nIf good befalls thee, it grieves them; but if a misfortune befalls thee, they say, “We took indeed our precautions beforehand,” and they turn away rejoicing. \nقُلْ لَّنْ يُّصِيْبَنَاۤ اِلَّا مَا كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَنَا ۚ هُوَ مَوْلٰٮنَا  ۚ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(51)\nQUL LAN-Y YYUSEEBANAA ILLAA MAA KATABAL LAAHO LANAA HOWA MAWLAANAA WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nSay: “Nothing will happen to us except what Allah has decreed for us: He is our protector”: and on Allah let the Believers put their trust. \nقُلْ هَلْ تَرَبَّصُوْنَ بِنَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِحْدَى الْحُسْنَيَيْنِؕ وَنَحْنُ نَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمْ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِعَذَابٍ مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖۤ اَوْ بِاَيْدِيْنَا  ۖ  فَتَرَبَّصُوْۤا اِنَّا مَعَكُمْ مُّتَرَبِّصُوْنَ‏(52)\nQUL HAL TARABBASOONA LAKHASAFA ILLAA EHDAB AL-HUSNAYAYNE WA NAHNO NATARABBASU BEKUM AN YYUSEEBAKUMU LAAHO BE-A’ZAABIN MIN I’NDEHI AW BE-AYDEENAA FATARABBASOOA INNAA MA-A’KUM MMUTARABBESOONA.\nSay: “Can you expect for us (any fate) other than one of two glorious things- (Martyrdom or victory)? But we can expect for you either that Allah will send his punishment from Himself, or by our hands. So wait (expectant); we too will wait with you.” \nقُلْ اَنْفِقُوْا طَوْعًا اَوْ كَرْهًا لَّنْ يُّتَقَبَّلَ مِنْكُمْؕ اِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(53)\nQUL ANFEQOO TEYAA AW AW LAN-Y YYUTAQABBALA MENKUM INNAKUM KUNTUM QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nSay: “Spend (for the cause) willingly or unwillingly: not from you will it be accepted: for ye are indeed a people rebellious and wicked.” \nوَمَا مَنَعَهُمْ اَنْ تُقْبَلَ مِنْهُمْ نَفَقٰتُهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَبِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَلَا يَاْتُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ اِلَّا وَهُمْ كُسَالٰى وَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ اِلَّا وَهُمْ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(54)\nWA MAA MANAA’AHUM AN TUQBALA MINHUM NAFAQAATUHUM ILLAA ANNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WABERASOOLEH WA LAA YAATOONAL SALAATA ILLAA WA HUM KUSAALAA WA LAA YUNFEQOONA ILLAA WA HUM KAAREHOONA.\nThe only reasons why their contributions are not accepted are: that they reject Allah and His Messenger; that they come to prayer without earnestness; and that they offer contributions unwillingly. \nفَلَا تُعْجِبْكَ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْؕ اِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمْ بِهَا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَتَزْهَقَ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(55)\nFALAA TUA’JEBKA AAMWAALUHUM WA LAA AAWLAADUHUM INNAMAA YOREEDO LAAHO LEEA’AZZEBAHUM BEHAA FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WATAZHAQA ANFOSOHUM WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nLet not their wealth nor their (following in) sons dazzle thee: in reality Allah's plan is to punish them with these things in this life, and that their souls may perish in their (very) denial of Allah. \nوَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ اِنَّهُمْ لَمِنْكُمْؕ وَمَا هُمْ مِّنْكُمْ وَلٰكِنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ يَّفْرَقُوْنَ‏(56)\nWAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE INNAHUM LAMENKUM WA MAA HUM MINKUM WALAAKENNAHUM QAWMUN YYAFRAQOONA.\nThey swear by Allah that they are indeed of you; but they are not of you: yet they are afraid (to appear in their true colours). \nلَوْ يَجِدُوْنَ مَلْجَاً اَوْ مَغٰرٰتٍ اَوْ مُدَّخَلًا لَّوَلَّوْا اِلَيْهِ وَهُمْ يَجْمَحُوْنَ‏(57)\nLAW YAJEDOONA MALJAA AW MAGHAARAATIN AW MUDDAKHALAN LLAWALLAWA ELAYHE WA HUM YAJMAHOONA.\nIf they could find a place to flee to, or caves, or a place of concealment, they would turn straightaway thereto, with an obstinate rush. \nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّلْمِزُكَ فِى الصَّدَقٰتِ ۚ فَاِنْ اُعْطُوْا مِنْهَا رَضُوْا وَاِنْ لَّمْ يُعْطَوْا مِنْهَاۤ اِذَا هُمْ يَسْخَطُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYALMEZUKA FIL SADAQAATE FA-IN AUA’TOOA MINHAA RAZOOA WA LAM YUA’TAWA MINHAA EZAA HUM YASKHATOONA.\nAnd among them are men who slander thee in the matter of (the distribution of) the alms: if they are given part thereof, they are pleased, but if not, behold! they are indignant! \nوَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ رَضُوْا مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗۙ وَقَالُوْا حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ سَيُؤْتِيْنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗۙ اِنَّاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ رٰغِبُوْنَ‏(59)\nWA LAW ANNAHUM RAZOOA MAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU WA QAALOO HASBUNAA LAAHO SAYUTEENAA LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI WA RASOOLUH INNAA ELAL LAAHE RAAGHEBOONA.\nIf only they had been content with what Allah and His Messenger gave them, and had said, “Sufficient unto us is Allah! Allah and His Messenger will soon give us of His bounty: to Allah do we turn our hopes!” (that would have been the right course). \nاِنَّمَا الصَّدَقٰتُ لِلْفُقَرَآءِ وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَالْعٰمِلِيْنَ عَلَيْهَا وَالْمُؤَلَّفَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَفِى الرِّقَابِ وَالْغٰرِمِيْنَ وَفِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِؕ فَرِيْضَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(60)\nINNAMAA AS-SADAQAATU LIL-FOQARAAA-IL WAL MASAAKEENE WA A’AMELEENAL A’LAYHAA WAL MUALLAFATE QULOOBUHUM WA FIR REQAAB WAL GHAAREMEENA WA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAB NIS SABEEL FAREEZATANW MENAL LAAH WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\n Alms are for the poor and the needy, and those employed to administer the (funds); for those whose hearts have been (recently) reconciled (to Truth); for those in bondage and in debt; in the cause of Allah; and for the wayfarer: (thus is it) ordained by Allah, and Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom. \nوَمِنْهُمُ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْذُوْنَ النَّبِىَّ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ هُوَ اُذُنٌ ؕ قُلْ اُذُنُ خَيْرٍ لَّكُمْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَيُؤْمِنُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَرَحْمَةٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْكُمْ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْذُوْنَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(61)\nWAMENHUMU LAZEENA YOAZOONAL NABIYYA WA YAQOOLOONA HOWA AUZUNUN QUL AUZUNU KHAYRIN LAKUM BIL LAAHE BIL-LAAHE WA BIL LAAHE LIL-MOAMENEEN WA RAHMAH LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO MINKUM WAL LAZEENA YOAZOONAL TOAZOO LAAHE LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nAmong them are men who molest the Prophet and say, “He is (all) ear.” Say, “He listens to what is best for you: he believes in Allah, has faith in the Believers, and is a Mercy to those of you who believe.” But those who molest the Messenger will have a grievous penalty. \nيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَكُمْ لِيُرْضُوْكُمْۚ وَاللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗۤ اَحَقُّ اَنْ يُّرْضُوْهُ اِنْ كَانُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(62)\nYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAKUM LEERZOOKUM WAL LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU AHAQQO AN YYURZOOHU IN KAANOO MUMENEENA.\nTo you they swear by Allah. In order to please you: But it is more fitting that they should please Allah and His Messenger, if they are Believers. \nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّهٗ مَنْ يُّحَادِدِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَاَنَّ لَهٗ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خَالِدًا فِيْهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْخِزْىُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(63)\nALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAHU MAN YYUHAADEDE LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU FA ANNAL LAHU NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDAN FEEHAA ZAA LEKA AL-KHEZAAU A’ZEEM.\nKnow they not that for those who oppose Allah and His Messenger, is the Fire of Hell? wherein they shall dwell. That is the supreme disgrace. \nيَحْذَرُ الْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ اَنْ تُنَزَّلَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُوْرَةٌ تُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ ؕ قُلِ اسْتَهْزِءُوْا ۚ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْرِجٌ مَّا تَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(64)\nYAHZARU MONAAFEQOONA AN TUNAZZALA A’LAYHIM SOORATUN TUNABBEUHUM BEMAA FEE QOLOOBEHIM QOLIL ASTAHZEOOA INNAL LAAHA MUKHREJUM MAA TAHZAROONA.\nThe Hypocrites are afraid lest a Sura should be sent down about them, showing them what is (really passing) in their hearts. Say: “Mock ye! But verily Allah will bring to light all that ye fear (should be revealed). \nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اِنَّمَا كُنَّا نَخُوْضُ وَنَلْعَبُؕ قُلْ اَبِاللّٰهِ وَاٰيٰتِهٖ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(65)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM LAYAQOOLUNNAL INNAMAA KUNNAA NAKHOOZU WANALA’ABU QUL AABEALLLAAHE WA AAYAATEHI WA RASOOLEHI KUNTUM TASTAHZEOONA.\nIf thou dost question them, they declare (with emphasis): “We were only talking idly and in play.” Say: “Was it at Allah, and His Signs, and His Messenger, that ye were mocking?” \nلَا تَعْتَذِرُوْا قَدْ كَفَرْتُمْ بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِكُمْ ؕ اِنْ نَّعْفُ عَنْ طَآئِفَةٍ مِّنْكُمْ نُعَذِّبْ طَآئِفَةً ۢ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(66)\nLAA TAA’TAZEROOA QAD KAFARTUM BA’DA EEMAANEKUM IN NNAA’FU A’N TAAEFATIN MINKUM NUA’AZZEB YASTAZ-E’FO BE-ANNAHUM KAANOO MUJREMEEN.\nMake ye no excuses: ye have rejected Faith after ye had accepted it. If We pardon some of you, We will punish others amongst you, for that they are in sin. \nاَلْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ وَالْمُنٰفِقٰتُ بَعْضُهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْضٍۘ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمُنْكَرِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَقْبِضُوْنَ اَيْدِيَهُمْؕ نَسُوا اللّٰهَ فَنَسِيَهُمْؕ اِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(67)\nAALMUNAAFEQOONA WAL MUNAAFEQAATU KHALAA MIN ELAA YAAMUROONA BIL-MUNKARE WAYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-MAA’ROOFE WAYAQBEZOONA AAYDEEHUM NASUL LAAHA FANASEEHUM INNAL MONAAFEQEENA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nThe Hypocrites, men and women, (have an understanding) with each other: They enjoin evil, and forbid what is just, and are close with their hands. They have forgotten Allah; so He hath forgotten them. Verily the Hypocrites are rebellious and perverse. \nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَالْمُنٰفِقٰتِ وَالْكُفَّارَ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ هِىَ حَسْبُهُمْ ۚ وَلَعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ ۙ‏(68)\nWA-A’DAR LAAHO MONAAFEQEENA WAL-MONAAFEQAATE WA KUFFAARA NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA HEYA HASBUHUM WA LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MMUQEEMUN.\nAllah hath promised the Hypocrites men and women, and the rejecters, of Faith, the fire of Hell: Therein shall they dwell: Sufficient is it for them: for them is the curse of Allah, and an enduring punishment, \nكَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ كَانُوْۤا اَشَدَّ مِنْكُمْ قُوَّةً وَّاَكْثَرَ اَمْوَالًا وَّاَوْلَادًا ؕ فَاسْتَمْتَعُوْا بِخَلَاقِهِمْ فَاسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِخَلَاقِكُمْ كَمَا اسْتَمْتَعَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ بِخَلَاقِهِمْ وَخُضْتُمْ كَالَّذِىْ خَاضُوْا ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(69)\nTAKOONOO MIN QABLEKUM KAANOO ASHADDA MINKUM QUWWAH WWAAKSARA AAMWAALAN WWAAWLAADAN FAASTAMTAU’OOA BEKHALAAQEHEM FAASTAMTAA’TUM BEKHALAAQEKUM KAMAA ASTAMTAA’A LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM BEKHALAAQEHEM WAKHUZTUM KALLAZEE KHAAZOOA AOOLAAEKA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nAs in the case of those before you: they were mightier than you in power, and more flourishing in wealth and children. They had their enjoyment of their portion: and ye have of yours, as did those before you; and ye indulge in idle talk as they did. They!- their work are fruitless in this world and in the Hereafter, and they will lose (all spiritual good). \nاَلَمْ يَاْتِهِمْ نَبَاُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ  ۙ وَقَوْمِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاَصْحٰبِ مَدْيَنَ وَالْمُؤْتَفِكٰتِ ؕ اَتَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ۚ فَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(70)\nALAM YAATEHEM NABAA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM QAWME NOOHIN WWAA’AADIN WA WA QAWME IBRAAHEEMA WA ASHAABIL MADYANA WAL MUTAFEKAATE AATATHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA KAANA LAAHO LE-YAZLEMAHUM WA LAAKIL KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nHath not the story reached them of those before them? the People of Noah, and 'Ad, and Thamud; the People of Abraham, the men of Midian, and the cities overthrown. To them came their messengers with clear signs. It is not Allah Who wrongs them, but they wrong their own souls. \nوَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتُ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍۘ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَيُطِيْعُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ سَيَرْحَمُهُمُ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(71)\nWAL MO’MENOONA WAL MUMENAATU KHALAA ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O ELAA YAAMUROONA BIL-MA’ROOF WAYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WAYUTEEU’OONA LAAHA WA RASOOLAH AOOLAAEKA SAYARHAMUHUMU LAAH INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nThe Believers, men and women, are protectors one of another: they enjoin what is just, and forbid what is evil: they observe regular prayers, practise regular charity, and obey Allah and His Messenger. On them will Allah pour His mercy: for Allah is Exalted in power, Wise. \nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا وَمَسٰكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِىْ جَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ ؕ وَرِضْوَانٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(72)\nWA-A’DAR LAAHO MOAMENEEN WAL-MOAMENAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WAMASAAKENA TAYBATAN FEE JANNATIN A’ADNIN WAREZWAANUN MENAL LAAHE AKBARO ZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nAllah hath promised to Believers, men and women, gardens under which rivers flow, to dwell therein, and beautiful mansions in gardens of everlasting bliss. But the greatest bliss is the good pleasure of Allah: that is the supreme felicity. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ جَاهِدِ الْكُفَّارَ وَالْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَاغْلُظْ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(73)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO JAAHEDE KUFFAARA KAAFEREENA WAAGHLUZ WA WA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA BEASAL MASEER.\nO Prophet! strive hard against the unbelievers and the Hypocrites, and be firm against them. Their abode is Hell, an evil refuge indeed. \nيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ مَا قَالُوْا ؕ وَلَقَدْ قَالُوْا كَلِمَةَ الْكُفْرِ وَكَفَرُوْا بَعْدَ اِسْلَامِهِمْ وَهَمُّوْا بِمَا لَمْ يَنَالُوْا ۚ وَمَا نَقَمُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ اَغْنٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ۚ فَاِنْ يَّتُوْبُوْا يَكُ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ يَّتَوَلَّوْا يُعَذِّبْهُمُ اللّٰهُ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا ۙ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَمَا لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(74)\nYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE MAA QAALOO WA LAQAD QAALOO KALEMATAT AL-KUFRE WA KAFAROO BA’DA AESLAAMEHEM WAHAMMOOA BEMAA LAM YANAALOO WA MAA NAQAMOO ILLAA AN AAGHNAAHUMU LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU MIN FAZLEHI FA-IN YYATOOBOOA YAKU KHAYRAN LAHUM WA YYATAWALLAWA YUA’AZZEBHUMU LAAHO A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WA MAA LAHUM FIL ARZE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nThey swear by Allah that they said nothing (evil), but indeed they uttered blasphemy, and they did it after accepting Islam; and they meditated a plot which they were unable to carry out: this revenge of theirs was (their) only return for the bounty with which Allah and His Messenger had enriched them! If they repent, it will be best for them; but if they turn back (to their evil ways), Allah will punish them with a grievous penalty in this life and in the Hereafter: They shall have none on earth to protect or help them. \nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ عَاهَدَ اللّٰهَ لَئِنْ اٰتٰٮنَا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ لَنَصَّدَّقَنَّ وَلَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(75)\nWA MINHUM MAN A’AAHADA LAAHA LAIL AAATAANAA MIN FAZLEHI LANASSADDAQANNA WALANAKOONANNA MENAL SAALEHEEN.\n Amongst them are men who made a covenant with Allah, that if He bestowed on them of His bounty, they would give (largely) in charity, and be truly amongst those who are righteous. \nفَلَمَّاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖ بَخِلُوْا بِهٖ وَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(76)\nFALAMMAA AAATAAHUM MIN FAZLEHI BAKHELOOA BEHI WA TAWALLAW WA HUM MO’REZOON.\nBut when He did bestow of His bounty, they became covetous, and turned back (from their covenant), averse (from its fulfilment). \nفَاَعْقَبَهُمْ نِفَاقًا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يَلْقَوْنَهٗ بِمَاۤ اَخْلَفُوا اللّٰهَ مَا وَعَدُوْهُ وَبِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْذِبُوْنَ‏(77)\nFAAA’QABAHUM NEFAAQAN FEE QOLOOBEHIM ELAA YAWMIL YALQAWNAHU BEMAA AAKHLAFOOA LAAHA MAA WAA’ADOOHU WA BEMAA KAANOO YAKZEBOON.\nSo He hath put as a consequence hypocrisy into their hearts, (to last) till the Day, whereon they shall meet Him: because they broke their covenant with Allah, and because they lied (again and again). \nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ سِرَّهُمْ وَنَجْوٰٮهُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ ۚ‏(78)\nALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO SERRAHUM WANAJWAAHUM WA ANNAL LAAHA A’ALLAAMU AL-GHUYOOBE.\nKnow they not that Allah doth know their secret (thoughts) and their secret counsels, and that Allah knoweth well all things unseen? \nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَلْمِزُوْنَ الْمُطَّوِّعِيْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ فِى الصَّدَقٰتِ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَجِدُوْنَ اِلَّا جُهْدَهُمْ فَيَسْخَرُوْنَ مِنْهُمْؕ سَخِرَ اللّٰهُ مِنْهُمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(79)\nLAZEENA YALMEZOONA AL-MUTTAWE’EENA MENAL MOAMENEEN FIL SADAQAATE WAL LAZEENA LAA YAJEDOONA ILLAA JUHDAHUM FAYASKHAROONA MENHUM SAKHERA LAAHO MINHUM WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThose who slander such of the believers as give themselves freely to (deeds of) charity, as well as such as can find nothing to give except the fruits of their labour, and throw ridicule on them, Allah will throw back their ridicule on them: and they shall have a grievous penalty. \nاِسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ اَوْ لَا تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْؕ اِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِيْنَ مَرَّةً فَلَنْ يَّغْفِرَ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْؕ ذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(80)\nAESTAGHFER LAHUM AW LAA TASTAGHFIR LAHUM IN TASTAGHFIR LAHUM SABE’EENA MARRATAN FALAN YAGHFERAL LAAHO LAHUM ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WARASOOLEH WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ FAASEQEEN.\nWhether thou ask for their forgiveness, or not, (their sin is unforgivable): if thou ask seventy times for their forgiveness, Allah will not forgive them: because they have rejected Allah and His Messenger: and Allah guideth not those who are perversely rebellious. \nفَرِحَ الْمُخَلَّفُوْنَ بِمَقْعَدِهِمْ خِلٰفَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَكَرِهُوْۤا اَنْ يُّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَقَالُوْا لَا تَنْفِرُوْا فِى الْحَرِّؕ قُلْ نَارُ جَهَنَّمَ اَشَدُّ حَرًّاؕ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(81)\nFAREHA MOKHALLAFOONA BEMAQA’ADEHEM KHELAAFA RASOOLIL LAAHE WAKAREHOOA AN YYUJAAHEDOOA BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA QAALOO LAA TANFEROOA FIL AL-HARR QUL NAARUL JAHANNAMA ASHADDO HARRAN LAW KAANOO YAFQAHOON.\nThose who were left behind (in the Tabuk expedition) rejoiced in their inaction behind the back of the Messenger of Allah: they hated to strive and fight, with their goods and their persons, in the cause of Allah: they said, “Go not forth in the heat.” Say, “The fire of Hell is fiercer in heat.” If only they could understand! \nفَلْيَضْحَكُوْا قَلِيْلاً وَّلْيَبْكُوْا كَثِيْرًا ۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(82)\nFALYAZHAKOOA QALEELAAN WWALYABKOOA KASEERAA JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nLet them laugh a little: much will they weep: a recompense for the (evil) that they do. \nفَاِنْ رَّجَعَكَ اللّٰهُ اِلٰى طَآئِفَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ فَاسْتَاْذَنُوْكَ لِلْخُرُوْجِ فَقُلْ لَّنْ تَخْرُجُوْا مَعِىَ اَبَدًا وَّلَنْ تُقَاتِلُوْا مَعِىَ عَدُوًّا ؕ اِنَّكُمْ رَضِيْتُمْ بِالْقُعُوْدِ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ فَاقْعُدُوْا مَعَ الْخٰلِفِيْنَ‏(83)\nFA-IN RRAJAA’AKA LAAHO ELAA TAAEFATIN MINHUM FAASTAAZANOOKA LIL-KHUROOJE FAQUL LAN-Y TAKHRUJOOA MA-E’YA ABADAM WWALAN TOQAATELOO MA-E’YA A’DUWWAL INNAKUM RAZEETUM BIL-QUU’OODE AWWALA MARRAH FAAQU’UDOOA LAAHA AL-KHAALEFEENA.\nIf, then, Allah bring thee back to any of them, and they ask thy permission to come out (with thee), say: “Never shall ye come out with me, nor fight an enemy with me: for ye preferred to sit inactive on the first occasion: Then sit ye (now) with those who lag behind.” \nوَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلٰٓى اَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ مَّاتَ اَبَدًا وَّلَا تَقُمْ عَلٰى قَبْرِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَ‏(84)\nWA LAA TUSALLE A’LAA AHADIM MINHUM MMAATA ABADAM WA LAA TAQUM A’LAA QABREH INNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA MAATOO WA HUM FAASEQOONA.\nNor do thou ever pray for any of them that dies, nor stand at his grave; for they rejected Allah and His Messenger, and died in a state of perverse rebellion. \nوَلَا تُعْجِبْكَ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَاَوْلَادُهُمْؕ اِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّعَذِّبَهُمْ بِهَا فِى الدُّنْيَا وَتَزْهَقَ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA LAA TUA’JEBKA AAMWAALUHUM WAAWLAADUHUM INNAMAA YOREEDO LAAHO AN YYUA’AZZEBAHUM BEHAA FIL DUNYAA WATAZHAQA ANFOSOHUM WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nNor let their wealth nor their (following in) sons dazzle thee: Allah's plan is to punish them with these things in this world, and that their souls may perish in their (very) denial of Allah. \nوَاِذَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ اَنْ اٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَجَاهِدُوْا مَعَ رَسُوْلِهِ اسْتَاْذَنَكَ اُولُوا الطَّوْلِ مِنْهُمْ وَقَالُوْا ذَرْنَا نَكُنْ مَّعَ الْقٰعِدِيْنَ‏(86)\nWA EZAA UNZELAT SOORATUN AN AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WAJAAHEDOOA LAAHA RASOOLEHE ASTAAZANAKA ULUL AT-TAWLE MINHUM WA QAALOO ZARNAA NAKUN MA-A’L AL-QAAE’EDEENA.\nWhen a Sura comes down, enjoining them to believe in Allah and to strive and fight along with His Messenger, those with wealth and influence among them ask thee for exemption, and say: “Leave us (behind): we would be with those who sit (at home).” \nرَضُوْا بِاَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الْخَوَالِفِ وَطُبِعَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(87)\nRAZOOA BOYOOTA YYAKOONOOA LAAHA AL-KHAWAALEFE WATUBEA’A A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FAHUM LAA YAFQAHOON.\nThey prefer to be with (the women), who remain behind (at home): their hearts are sealed and so they understand not. \nلٰكِنِ الرَّسُوْلُ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ جَاهَدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمُ الْخَيْرٰتُ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(88)\nLAAKENE RASOOLO WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU JAAHADOO BEAAMWAALEHEM WAANFUSEHEM WAAWLAAEKA LAHOMUL AL-KHAYRAATU WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nBut the Messenger, and those who believe with him, strive and fight with their wealth and their persons: for them are (all) good things: and it is they who will prosper. \nاَعَدَّ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(89)\nA-A’DDA LAAHO LAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ZAA LEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nAllah hath prepared for them gardens under which rivers flow, to dwell therein: that is the supreme felicity. \nوَ جَآءَ الْمُعَذِّرُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ لِيُؤْذَنَ لَهُمْ وَقَعَدَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ؕ سَيُصِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(90)\nWA JAAA-A AL-MUA’AZZEROONA MENAL A-A’RAABE LEEZANA LAHUM WAQAA’ADA LAZEENA KAZABOOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU SAYUSEEBU LAZEENA KAFAROO MINHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nAnd there were, among the desert Arabs (also), men who made excuses and came to claim exemption; and those who were false to Allah and His Messenger (merely) sat inactive. Soon will a grievous penalty seize the Unbelievers among them. \nلَيْسَ عَلَى الضُّعَفَآءِ وَلَا عَلَى الْمَرْضٰى وَلَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَجِدُوْنَ مَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ حَرَجٌ اِذَا نَصَحُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَ رَسُوْلِهٖؕ مَا عَلَى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ مِنْ سَبِيْلٍؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ‏(91)\nLAYSA A’LAL AZ-ZUA’AFAAE WA LAA A’LAL AL-MARZAA WA LAA A’LAL LAZEENA LAA YAJEDOONA MAA YUNFEQOONA HARAJUN EZAA NASAHOOA LILLAAHE WA RASOOLEH MAA A’LAL MOHSENEEN MIN SABEELIN WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nThere is no blame on those who are infirm, or ill, or who find no resources to spend (on the cause), if they are sincere (in duty) to Allah and His Messenger: no ground (of complaint) can there be against such as do right: and Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَّلَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا مَاۤ اَتَوْكَ لِتَحْمِلَهُمْ قُلْتَ لَاۤ اَجِدُ مَاۤ اَحْمِلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ تَوَلَّوْا وَّاَعْيُنُهُمْ تَفِيْضُ مِنَ الدَّمْعِ حَزَنًا اَلَّا يَجِدُوْا مَا يُنْفِقُوْنَؕ‏(92)\nWA LAA A’LAL LAZEENA EZAA MAA AATAWKA LETAHMELAHUM QULTA LAA AAJEDU MAA AAHMELUKUM A’LAYHE TAWALLAW WWAAA’YUNUHUM TAFEEZU MENAL AD-DAME’E HAZANAN ALLAA YAJEDOOA MAA ZAA YUNFEQOON.\nNor (is there blame) on those who came to thee to be provided with mounts, and when thou saidst, “I can find no mounts for you,” they turned back, their eyes streaming with tears of grief that they had no resources wherewith to provide the expenses. \nاِنَّمَا السَّبِيْلُ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَاْذِنُوْنَكَ وَهُمْ اَغْنِيَآءُۚ رَضُوْا بِاَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الْخَوَالِفِۙ وَطَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(93)\nINNAMAA AS-SABEELU A’LAL LAZEENA YASTAAZENOONAKA WA HUM AAGHNEEAAAU RAZOOA BOYOOTA YYAKOONOOA LAAHA AL-KHAWAALEFE WATABAA’A LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\n The ground (of complaint) is against such as claim exemption while they are rich. They prefer to stay with the (women) who remain behind: Allah hath sealed their hearts; so they know not (What they miss). \nيَعْتَذِرُوْنَ اِلَيْكُمْ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ ؕ قُلْ لَّا تَعْتَذِرُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لَكُمْ قَدْ نَبَّاَنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْ اَخْبَارِكُمْ ؕ وَ سَيَرَى اللّٰهُ عَمَلَكُمْ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ ثُمَّ تُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(94)\nYAA’TAZEROONA ELAYKUM EZAA RAJAA’TUM ELAYHIM QUL LAA TAA’TAZEROOA LAN NOAMENA LAKUM QAD NABBAANAA LAAHO MIN AAKHBAAREKUM WA SA-YARAL LAAHO A’AMALAKUM WA RASOOLOHU SUMMA TORADDOONA ELAA A’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThey will present their excuses to you when ye return to them. Say thou: “Present no excuses: we shall not believe you: Allah hath already informed us of the true state of matters concerning you: It is your actions that Allah and His Messenger will observe: in the end will ye be brought back to Him Who knoweth what is hidden and what is open: then will He show you the truth of all that ye did.” \nسَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اِذَا انْقَلَبْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ لِتُعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمْؕ فَاَعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمْؕ اِنَّهُمْ رِجْسٌ وَّمَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(95)\nSAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAKUM EZAA ANQALABTUM ELAYHIM LETUA’REZOOA A’ANHUM FAAA’REZOOA A’ANHUM INNAHUM REJSUN WWAMAAWAAHUM JAHANNAMUL JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nThey will swear to you by Allah, when ye return to them, that ye may leave them alone. So leave them alone: For they are an abomination, and Hell is their dwelling-place, a fitting recompense for the (evil) that they did. \nيَحْلِفُوْنَ لَكُمْ لِتَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْۚ فَاِنْ تَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَرْضٰى عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(96)\nYAHLEFOONA LAKUM LETARZAWA A’NHUM FA-IN TARZAWA A’NHUM FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YARZAA A’NIL QAWMIL FAASEQEEN.\nThey will swear unto you, that ye may be pleased with them but if ye are pleased with them, Allah is not pleased with those who disobey. \nاَلْاَعْرَابُ اَشَدُّ كُفْرًا وَّ نِفَاقًا وَّاَجْدَرُ اَلَّا يَعْلَمُوْا حُدُوْدَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(97)\nAALAAA’RAABU ASHADDO KUFRAN WA NEFAAQAN WWAAJDARU ALLAA YAA’LAMOOA HODOODAL MAA ANZALAL LAAHO A’LAA RASOOLEH WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nThe Arabs of the desert are the worst in Unbelief and hypocrisy, and most fitted to be in ignorance of the command which Allah hath sent down to His Messenger: But Allah is All-knowing, All-Wise. \nوَمِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مَنْ يَّتَّخِذُ مَا يُنْفِقُ مَغْرَمًا وَّيَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمُ الدَّوَآئِرَؕ عَلَيْهِمْ دَآئِرَةُ السَّوْءِؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(98)\nWA MENAN A-A’RAABE MAN YATTAKHEZO MAA YUNFEQO MAGHRAMAN WWAYATARABBASU BEKOMUL AD-DAWAAERA A’LAYHIM DAA-ERATUS SAW WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nSome of the desert Arabs look upon their payments as a fine, and watch for disasters for you: on them be the disaster of evil: for Allah is He That heareth and knoweth (all things). \nوَمِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَيَتَّخِذُ مَا يُنْفِقُ قُرُبٰتٍ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَصَلَوٰتِ الرَّسُوْلِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهَا قُرْبَةٌ لَّهُمْؕ سَيُدْخِلُهُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(99)\nWA MENAN A-A’RAABE MAN YOAMENO BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WAYATTAKHEZU MAA YUNFEQO QURUBAATIN I’NDAL LAAHE WASALAWTE AR-RASOOLE ALAA INNAHAA QURBATUN LAHUM SAYUDKHELUHUMU LAAHO FEE FEE INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nBut some of the desert Arabs believe in Allah and the Last Day, and look on their payments as pious gifts bringing them nearer to Allah and obtaining the prayers of the Messenger. Aye, indeed they bring them nearer (to Him): soon will Allah admit them to His Mercy: for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَالسّٰبِقُوْنَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُهٰجِرِيْنَ وَالْاَنْصَارِ وَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْهُمْ بِاِحْسَانٍ ۙ رَّضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ وَاَعَدَّ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ تَحْتَهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(100)\nWAS-SAABEQOONAS AWWALOON MENAL MOHAAJEREENAL WAL AANSAARE WAL LAZEENA ATTABAU’OOHUM BE-EHSAAN RRAZEAAA LAAHO A’NHUM WARAZOOA A’NHO WA A-A’DDA LAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE TAHTAHAA ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM ZAA LEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nThe vanguard (of Islam)- the first of those who forsook (their homes) and of those who gave them aid, and (also) those who follow them in (all) good deeds, well-pleased is Allah with them, as are they with Him: for them hath He prepared gardens under which rivers flow, to dwell therein for ever: that is the supreme felicity. \nوَمِمَّنْ حَوْلَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مُنٰفِقُوْنَ ۛؕ وَمِنْ اَهْلِ الْمَدِيْنَةِ  ؔۛمَرَدُوْا عَلَى النِّفَاقِلَا تَعْلَمُهُمْ ؕ نَحْنُ نَعْلَمُهُمْ ؕ سَنُعَذِّبُهُمْ مَّرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عَذَابٍ عَظِيْمٍ ۚ‏(101)\nWA MIMMAN HAWLAKUM MENAL A-A’RAABE MUNAAFEQOONA WA MIN AHLIL MADEENATE MARADOOA A’LAL AN-NEFAAQELAA TAA’LAMUHUM NAHNO NAA’LAMUHUM SANUA’AZZEBUHUM MARRATAYNE SUMMA YORADDOONA ELAA A’ZAABIN A’ZEEM.\nCertain of the desert Arabs round about you are hypocrites, as well as (desert Arabs) among the Medina folk: they are obstinate in hypocrisy: thou knowest them not: We know them: twice shall We punish them: and in addition shall they be sent to a grievous penalty. \nوَاٰخَرُوْنَ اعْتَرَفُوْا بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ خَلَطُوْا عَمَلًا صَالِحًا وَّاٰخَرَ سَيِّئًا ؕ عَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّتُوْبَ عَلَيْهِمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(102)\nWA AAKHAROONA AA’TARAFOOA BEZUNOOBEHEM KHALATOOA A’AMALAN SAALEHAN WWAAKHARA SAYAN A’ASAA LAAHO AN YYATOOBA A’LAYHIM INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nOthers (there are who) have acknowledged their wrong-doings: they have mixed an act that was good with another that was evil. Perhaps Allah will turn unto them (in Mercy): for Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful. \nخُذْ مِنْ اَمْوَالِهِمْ صَدَقَةً تُطَهِّرُهُمْ وَتُزَكِّيْهِمْ بِهَا وَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْؕ اِنَّ صَلٰوتَكَ سَكَنٌ لَّهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(103)\nKHUZ MIN AAMWAALEHEM SADAQATAN TUTAHHERUHUM WATUZAKKEEHEM BEHAA WASALLE WA INNAL SALAAWTAKA SAKANUN LAHUM WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nOf their goods, take alms, that so thou mightest purify and sanctify them; and pray on their behalf. Verily thy prayers are a source of security for them: And Allah is One Who heareth and knoweth. \nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ يَقْبَلُ التَّوْبَةَ عَنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَاْخُذُ الصَّدَقٰتِ وَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(104)\nALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA HOWA YAQBALU AT-TAWBATA A’N E’BAADEHI WAYAAKHUZU SADAQAATE WA ANNAL LAAHA HOWA TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nKnow they not that Allah doth accept repentance from His votaries and receives their gifts of charity, and that Allah is verily He, the Oft-Returning, Most Merciful? \nوَقُلِ اعْمَلُوْا فَسَيَرَى اللّٰهُ عَمَلَكُمْ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَؕ وَسَتُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۚ‏(105)\nWA AA’MALOOA FASAYARAA LAAHO A’AMALAKUM WA RASOOLOHU WA KULLUN WASATURADDOONA ELAA A’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd say: “Work (righteousness): Soon will Allah observe your work, and His Messenger, and the Believers: Soon will ye be brought back to the knower of what is hidden and what is open: then will He show you the truth of all that ye did.” \nوَاٰخَرُوْنَ مُرْجَوْنَ لِاَمْرِ اللّٰهِ اِمَّا يُعَذِّبُهُمْ وَاِمَّا يَتُوْبُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(106)\nWA AAKHAROONA MURJAWNA LE-AMRE LAAHE IMMAA YUA’AZZEBUHUM WA AMMAA YATOOBU WA WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nThere are (yet) others, held in suspense for the command of Allah, whether He will punish them, or turn in mercy to them: and Allah is All-Knowing, Wise. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مَسْجِدًا ضِرَارًا وَّكُفْرًا وَّتَفْرِيْقًۢا بَيْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَاِرْصَادًا لِّمَنْ حَارَبَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَلَيَحْلِفُنَّ اِنْ اَرَدْنَاۤ اِلَّا الْحُسْنٰىؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَشْهَدُ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(107)\nWAL LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA MASJEDAN ZERAARAL WWAKUFRAN WWATAFREEQAN BAYNA MOAMENEEN WAARSAADAN LEMAN HAARABA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU MIN QABL WA WALAYAHLEFUNNA IN AARADNAA ILLAA HUSNAA WAL LAAHO YASHHADO INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nAnd there are those who put up a mosque by way of mischief and infidelity - to disunite the Believers - and in preparation for one who warred against Allah and His Messenger aforetime. They will indeed swear that their intention is nothing but good; But Allah doth declare that they are certainly liars. \nلَا تَقُمْ فِيْهِ اَبَدًا ؕ لَمَسْجِدٌ اُسِّسَ عَلَى التَّقْوٰى مِنْ اَوَّلِ يَوْمٍ اَحَقُّ اَنْ تَقُوْمَ فِيْهِؕ فِيْهِ رِجَالٌ يُّحِبُّوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَطَهَّرُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُطَّهِّرِيْنَ‏(108)\nLAA TAQUM FEEHE ABADAM LAMASJEDUN AUSSESA A’LAL TAQWAA MIN AAWLE YAWMIN AHAQQO AN TAQOOMA FEEH FEEHE REJAALUN YYUHEBBOONA AN YYATATAHHAROOA WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL AL-MUTTAHHEREENA.\nNever stand thou forth therein. There is a mosque whose foundation was laid from the first day on piety; it is more worthy of the standing forth (for prayer) therein. In it are men who love to be purified; and Allah loveth those who make themselves pure. \nاَفَمَنْ اَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهٗ عَلٰى تَقْوٰى مِنَ اللّٰهِ وَرِضْوَانٍ خَيْرٌ اَمْ مَّنْ اَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهٗ عَلٰى شَفَا جُرُفٍ هَارٍ فَانْهَارَ بِهٖ فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(109)\nAFAMAWN AASSASA BUNYAANAH A’LAA TAQWAA MENAL LAAHE WAREZWAANIN KHAYRUL AM MAN AASSASA BUNYAANAH A’LAA SHAFAA JURUFIN HAARIN FAANHAARA BEHI FEE NAARE JAHANNAM WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nWhich then is best? - he that layeth his foundation on piety to Allah and His good pleasure? - or he that layeth his foundation on an undermined sand-cliff ready to crumble to pieces? and it doth crumble to pieces with him, into the fire of Hell. And Allah guideth not people that do wrong. \nلَا يَزَالُ بُنْيَانُهُمُ الَّذِىْ بَنَوْا رِيْبَةً فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَقَطَّعَ قُلُوْبُهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(110)\nLAA YAZAALU BUNYAANUHUMU LAZEE BANAWA REEBATAN FEE QOLOOBEHIM ILLAA AN TAQATTAA’A QOLOOBOHUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nThe foundation of those who so build is never free from suspicion and shakiness in their hearts, until their hearts are cut to pieces. And Allah is All-Knowing, Wise. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ اشْتَرٰى مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَاَمْوَالَهُمْ بِاَنَّ لَهُمُ الْجَنَّةَ ؕ يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَيَقْتُلُوْنَ وَ يُقْتَلُوْنَوَعْدًا عَلَيْهِ حَقًّا فِى التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَالْاِنْجِيْلِ وَالْقُرْاٰنِ ؕ وَمَنْ اَوْفٰى بِعَهْدِهٖ مِنَ اللّٰهِ فَاسْتَبْشِرُوْا بِبَيْعِكُمُ الَّذِىْ بَايَعْتُمْ بِهٖ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(111)\nINNAL LAAHA ASHTARAA MENAL MOAMENEEN ANFOSAHUM WA AMWAALAHUM BE-ANNAL LAHOMUL JANNATA YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FAYAQTULOONA WA YUQTALOONAWAA’DAN A’LAYHE HAQQAN FIL WA WA INJEELE WAL QURAANIL WA MAN AWFAA BEA’AHDEH MENAL LAAHE FAASTABSHEROOA BEBAYE’EKUMU LAZEE BAAYAA’TUM BEHI WAZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\n Allah hath purchased of the believers their persons and their goods; for theirs (in return) is the garden (of Paradise): they fight in His cause, and slay and are slain: a promise binding on Him in truth, through the Law, the Gospel, and the Qur'an: and who is more faithful to his covenant than Allah? then rejoice in the bargain which ye have concluded: that is the achievement supreme. \nاَلتَّاۤئِبُوْنَ الْعٰبِدُوْنَ الْحٰمِدُوْنَ السّاۤئِحُوْنَ الرّٰكِعُوْنَ السّٰجِدُوْنَ الْاٰمِرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَالنَّاهُوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَالْحٰفِظُوْنَ لِحُدُوْدِ اللّٰه ِؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nAALTTAAEBOONA AL-A’AABEDOONA AL-HAAMEDOONA AS-SAEHOONA AR-RAAKEU’OONA AS-SAAJEDOONA AL-AAAMEROONA BIL-MA’ROOF WAALNNAAHOONA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WAL HAAFEZOONA LEHUDOODE AL-LAAH WA BASH-SHERIL MOAMENEEN.\nThose that turn (to Allah) in repentance; that serve Him, and praise Him; that wander in devotion to the cause of Allah,: that bow down and prostrate themselves in prayer; that enjoin good and forbid evil; and observe the limit set by Allah;- (These do rejoice). So proclaim the glad tidings to the Believers. \nمَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِىِّ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْاۤ اَنْ يَّسْتَغْفِرُوْا لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ وَ لَوْ كَانُوْۤا اُولِىْ قُرْبٰى مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ اَنَّهُمْ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(113)\nMAA KAANA MOAMENATAN INW WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AN YYASTAGHFEROOA LIL-MUSHREKEENA WA LAW KAANOO OOLEE QURBAA MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHUM ANNAHUM ASHAABUN JAHEEM.\nIt is not fitting, for the Prophet and those who believe, that they should pray for forgiveness for Pagans, even though they be of kin, after it is clear to them that they are companions of the Fire. \nوَمَا كَانَ اسْتِغْفَارُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لِاَبِيْهِ اِلَّا عَنْ مَّوْعِدَةٍ وَّعَدَهَاۤ اِيَّاهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهٗۤ اَنَّهٗ عَدُوٌّ لِّلّٰهِ تَبَرَّاَ مِنْهُ ؕ اِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لَاَوَّاهٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(114)\nWA MAA KAANA ASTEGHFAARU IBRAAHEEMA LEAABEEHE ILLAA A’N MMAWE’EDATIN WWAA’ADAHAA IYYAAHO FALAMMAA TABAYYANA LAHU ANNAHU A’DUWWUM LILLAAHE TABARRA-AL MINHO INNAL IBRAAHEEMA LAAWWAAHUN HALEEM.\nAnd Abraham prayed for his father's forgiveness only because of a promise he had made to him. But when it became clear to him that he was an enemy to Allah, he dissociated himself from him: for Abraham was most tender-hearted, forbearing. \nوَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُضِلَّ قَوْمًۢا بَعْدَ اِذْ هَدٰٮهُمْ حَتّٰى يُبَيِّنَ لَهُمْ مَّا يَتَّقُوْنَؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(115)\nWA MAA KAANA LAAHO LEEZELLA QAWMAN BA’DA IZ HADAAHUM HATTAA YUBAYNA LAHUM MAA YATTAQOONA INNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nAnd Allah will not mislead a people after He hath guided them, in order that He may make clear to them what to fear (and avoid)- for Allah hath knowledge of all things. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُؕ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(116)\nINNAL LAAHA LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ YOHYEE WA YOMEET WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nUnto Allah belongeth the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He giveth life and He taketh it. Except for Him ye have no protector nor helper. \nلَقَدْ تَّابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَى النَّبِىِّ وَالْمُهٰجِرِيْنَ وَالْاَنْصَارِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْهُ فِىْ سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيْغُ قُلُوْبُ فَرِيْقٍ مِّنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْؕ اِنَّهٗ بِهِمْ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ ‏(117)\nLAQAD TTAABA LAAHO A’LAL NESAAA-AN WA MOHAAJEREENAL WAL AANSAARE LAZEENA ATTABAU’OOHU FEE SAAA’ATE AL-U’USRATE MIN BA’DE MAA KAADA YAZEEGHU QULOOBU FAREEQIN MINHUM SUMMA TAABA WA INNAHU BEHIM RA-OOFUM RAHEEM.\nAllah turned with favour to the Prophet, the Muhajirs, and the Ansar, who followed him in a time of distress, after that the hearts of a part of them had nearly swerved (from duty); but He turned to them (also): for He is unto them Most Kind, Most Merciful. \nوَّعَلَى الثَّلٰثَةِ الَّذِيْنَ خُلِّفُوْا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنْ لَّا مَلْجَاَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِلَّاۤ اِلَيْهِ ؕ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوْبُوْا  ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(118)\nWWAA’ALAA AS-SALAASATE LAZEENA KHULLEFOOA HATTAA EZAA ZAAQAT A’LAYHEMUL ARZO BEMAA RAHUBAT WAZAAQAT A’LAYHIM ANFOSOHUM WA ZANNOO AN LAA MALJAA MENAL LAAHE ILLAA ELAYHE SUMMA TAABA A’LAYHIM LE-YATOOBOO INNAL LAAHA HOWA TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\n(He turned in mercy also) to the three who were left behind; (they felt guilty) to such a degree that the earth seemed constrained to them, for all its spaciousness, and their (very) souls seemed straitened to them, and they perceived that there is no fleeing from Allah (and no refuge) but to Himself. Then He turned to them, that they might repent: for Allah is Oft-Returning, Most Merciful. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(119)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQUL LAAHA WA KOONOO LAAHA SAADEQEENA.\nO ye who believe! Fear Allah and be with those who are true (in word and deed). \nمَا كَانَ لِاَهْلِ الْمَدِيْنَةِ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَعْرَابِ اَنْ يَّتَخَلَّفُوْا عَنْ رَّسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَ لَا يَرْغَبُوْا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ لَا يُصِيْبُهُمْ ظَمَاٌ وَّلَا نَصَبٌ وَّلَا مَخْمَصَةٌ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا يَطَئُوْنَ مَوْطِئًا يَّغِيْظُ الْكُفَّارَ وَلَا يَنَالُوْنَ مِنْ عَدُوٍّ نَّيْلاً اِلَّا كُتِبَ لَهُمْ بِهٖ عَمَلٌ صَالِحٌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَۙ‏(120)\nMAA KAANA LE-AHLIL MADEENATE WA MAN HAWLAHUM MENAL A-A’RAABE AN YYATAKHALLAFOOA A’N RRASOOLE LAAHE WA LAA YARGHABOOA BE-ANFOSEHIM A’N NNAFSEH ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM LAA YUSEEBUHUM ZAMAA WA LAA NASABUN WA LAA MAKHMASATUN FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAA YATAOONA MAWTEAN YYAGHEEZU KUFFAARA WA LAA YANAALOONA MIN A’ADOO NNAYLAAN ILLAA KOTEBA LAHUM BEHI A’AMALUN SAALEHUN INNAL LAAHA LAA YUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nIt was not fitting for the people of Medina and the Bedouin Arabs of the neighbourhood, to refuse to follow Allah's Messenger, nor to prefer their own lives to his: because nothing could they suffer or do, but was reckoned to their credit as a deed of righteousness, whether they suffered thirst, or fatigue, or hunger, in the cause of Allah, or trod paths to raise the ire of the Unbelievers, or received any injury whatever from an enemy: for Allah suffereth not the reward to be lost of those who do good;- \nوَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ نَفَقَةً صَغِيْرَةً وَّلَا كَبِيْرَةً وَّلَا يَقْطَعُوْنَ وَادِيًا اِلَّا كُتِبَ لَهُمْ لِيَجْزِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ اَحْسَنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(121)\nWA LAA YUNFEQOONA NAFAQATAN SAGHEERATAN WA LAA KABEERATAN WA LAA YAQTAU’OONA WAADEEA ILLAA KOTEBA LAHUM LEEJZEEHUMU LAAHO AHSANAL MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nNor could they spend anything (for the cause) - small or great- nor cut across a valley, but the deed is inscribed to their credit: that Allah may requite their deed with the best (possible reward). \nوَمَا كَانَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ لِيَنْفِرُوْا كَآفَّةً ؕ فَلَوْلَا نَفَرَ مِنْ كُلِّ فِرْقَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ طَآئِفَةٌ لِّيَتَفَقَّهُوْا فِى الدِّيْنِ وَ لِيُنْذِرُوْا قَوْمَهُمْ اِذَا رَجَعُوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(122)\nWA MAA KAANA MOAMENOONA LEENFEROOA KAAAF-FATANW FA-LAWLAA NAFARA MIN KULLE FERQATIN MINHUM TAAEFATUN LLEETAFAQQAHOOA FIL DEENE WA LEENZEROOA QAWMAHUM EZAA RAJAU’OOA ELAYHIM LA-A’LLAHUM YAHZAROON.\n Nor should the Believers all go forth together: if a contingent from every expedition remained behind, they could devote themselves to studies in religion, and admonish the people when they return to them, that thus they (may learn) to guard themselves (against evil). \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا قَاتِلُوا الَّذِيْنَ يَلُوْنَكُمْ مِّنَ الْكُفَّارِ وَلْيَجِدُوْا فِيْكُمْ غِلْظَةً  ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْاۤ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(123)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO QAATELOOA LAZEENA YALOONAKUM MENAL KUFFAARE WALYAJEDOOA FEEKUM GHELZATAN WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA LAAHA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nO ye who believe! fight the unbelievers who gird you about, and let them find firmness in you: and know that Allah is with those who fear Him. \nوَاِذَا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّقُوْلُ اَيُّكُمْ زَادَتْهُ هٰذِهٖۤ اِيْمَانًا ۚ فَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فَزَادَتْهُمْ اِيْمَانًا وَّهُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ‏(124)\nWA EZAA MAA UNZELAT SOORATUN FA-MINHUM MAN YAQOOLO AYYOKUM ZAADATHU HAAZEHI EEMAANAW FA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO FAZAADATHUM EEMAANAW WA HUM YASTABSHEROON.\nWhenever there cometh down a sura, some of them say: “Which of you has had His faith increased by it?” Yea, those who believe, their faith is increased and they do rejoice. \nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ فَزَادَتْهُمْ رِجْسًا اِلٰى رِجْسِهِمْ وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(125)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN FAZAADATHUM REJSAN ELAA REJSEHEM WA MAATOO WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nBut those in whose hearts is a disease, it will add doubt to their doubt, and they will die in a state of Unbelief. \nاَوَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ يُفْتَنُوْنَ فِىْ كُلِّ عَامٍ مَّرَّةً اَوْ مَرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ لَا يَتُوْبُوْنَ وَلَا هُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(126)\nAWA LAA YARAWNAL ANNAHUM LAA YUFTANOON FEE KULLE FAN-ZUR MMARRATAN AW MARRATAYNE SUMMA LAA YATOOBOONA WA LAA HUM YAZZAKKAROONA.\nSee they not that they are tried every year once or twice? Yet they turn not in repentance, and they take no heed. \nوَاِذَا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ نَّظَرَ بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍؕ هَلْ يَرٰٮكُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ ثُمَّ انْصَرَفُوْا ؕ صَرَفَ اللّٰهُ قُلُوْبَهُمْ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(127)\nWA EZAA MAA UNZELAT SOORATUN NNAZARA KHALAA ELAA BA’Z WA HAL YARAAKUM MIN AHADIM SUMMA ANSARAFOOA SARAFA LAAHO QULOOBAHUM BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUN LAA YAFQAHOON.\nWhenever there cometh down a Sura, they look at each other, (saying), “Doth anyone see you?” Then they turn aside: Allah hath turned their hearts (from the light); for they are a people that understand not. \nلَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ عَزِيْزٌ عَلَيْهِ مَا عَنِتُّمْ حَرِيْصٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(128)\nLAQAD JAAA-AKUM RASOOLUM MIN ANFOSEKUM A’ZEEZUN A’LAYHE MAA A’ANETTUM HAREESUN A’LAYKUM BIL-MOAMENEENA RA-OOFUM RAHEEM.\nNow hath come unto you a Messenger from amongst yourselves: it grieves him that ye should perish: ardently anxious is he over you: to the Believers is he most kind and merciful. \nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُلْ حَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ ۖ  لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ ؕ وَهُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(129)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FA-QUL HASBEYAL LAAH, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTO WA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL A’ZEEM. (129)\n129. But if they turn away, Say: “Allah sufficeth me: there is no god but He: On Him is my trust, He the Lord of the Throne (of Glory) Supreme!” ",
  "merits": "This Surah has 129 verses and was revealed in Madinah. This Surah was revealed all at once and its revelation was accompanied by seventy thousand angels. It is narrated that keeping this Surah over one’s head (like in a cap or Amama) is a safety from thieves and destruction of property by fire. Also, keeping this Surah in one’s possession ensures safety from the evil designs of enemies."
